  "notes": "Both covenants are tested quarterly, starting with the Measurement Period ending September 26, 2025. The Third Amendment (June 8, 2026) restated both covenants; the amended text is quoted above.\n\nLeverage covenant:\n- The base maximum is 4.00x, previously 3.75x.\n- At the Borrowers' election, the limit rises to 4.50x (previously 4.25x) for the four consecutive quarters after a Designated Acquisition, meaning a Permitted Acquisition with consideration of at least $50M.\n- This holiday may be used no more than twice.\n- Despite its name, the 'Consolidated Leverage Ratio' is a net ratio. It nets unrestricted cash and Cash Equivalents of Loan Parties, cash held with the Agent or Lenders or in the US, and cash pledged to the Secured Parties, capped at $100M.\n\nFixed charge coverage covenant:\n- The minimum is 1.00x for the four fiscal quarters after the Specified Acquisition closes, then reverts to 1.25x.\n- The Specified Acquisition is the equity purchase under the June 8, 2026 Equity Purchase Agreement with Runway Midco/Runway Buyer.\n- The 1.00x step is tied to a closing that had not occurred as of the amendment date, so no calendar date is recorded for it.\n- Numerator: EBITDA less cash capex less cash taxes.\n- Denominator: cash interest, scheduled amortization (deemed paid even if prepaid), other scheduled debt payments, and Restricted Payments under 7.06(d).\n\nThe interest coverage slot in 7.10(a) is [Reserved].\n\nOther Third Amendment changes:\n- Deferred purchase price and non-contingent seller debt for the Specified Acquisition is excluded from Consolidated Funded Indebtedness unless unpaid 10 Business Days after it falls due.\n- A new pricing level 5 applies above 3.75x leverage: SOFR+2.00% and Base Rate+1.00%.\n\nConsolidated EBITDA add-backs:\n- Acquisition expenses, capped at 15% of EBITDA.\n- Unusual or non-recurring charges including restructuring, capped at 25%.\n- Run-rate cost savings and synergies from Specified Transactions over a 12-month window, capped at 15%.\n- Non-Cash Charges, which include impairments and write-downs, equity-method losses, purchase accounting, mark-to-market hedging losses, non-cash disposition losses and stock-based compensation. This category is uncapped.\n\nThe 2026 delayed draw term loans (Second Amendment, May 15, 2026) require pro forma compliance with Section 7.10 at each funding.\n\nPro forma compliance with 7.10 is also used as an incurrence test for:\n- Permitted Acquisitions, where a Designated Acquisition is tested at 4.25x per the unamended text of 7.03(j);\n- restricted payments under 7.06(h);\n- other investments under 7.03(p);\n- unsecured debt under 7.02(n).\nThese incurrence tests are not separate maintenance covenants.\n\nRequired Lenders alone can amend the financial covenants.\n\nThere is no unrestricted subsidiary concept; all subsidiaries are restricted.",
  "terms": [
