      "section": "Section 1.01 (Pluralsight Protection); Sections 7.03 and 7.05",
      "quote": "no Loan Party may transfer legal title to, or otherwise dispose of, or license on an exclusive basis (excluding exclusive licenses limited by territory or field of use), any Material IP Rights to a Subsidiary that is not a Loan Party, if the primary purpose of such transfer or license is to incur new financing at such Subsidiary that is not a Loan Party and to cause a release of the Liens on the Collateral on such Material IP Rights, in each case as reasonably determined by the Lead Borrower.",
      "summary": "There are no unrestricted subsidiaries. A 'Pluralsight Protection' bars Investments and Dispositions that transfer or exclusively license material IP to non-Loan Party subsidiaries. It applies only where the primary purpose is to raise new financing there and release the collateral liens, as determined by the borrower.",
      "quote_verified": true
    },
    {
      "kind": "serta_protection",
      "present": "yes",
      "section": "Section 11.01(k)",
      "quote": "contractually subordinate the Liens of the Administrative Agent on all or substantially all of the Collateral to the Liens on the collateral securing any other indebtedness for borrowed money",
      "summary": "Contractually subordinating the liens on all or substantially all collateral, or subordinating payment rights, to other borrowed-money debt requires consent of each directly and adversely affected Lender. The exception is where each such Lender was offered a bona fide pro rata opportunity to provide the senior debt on the same terms. DIP-type post-bankruptcy debt is excluded.",
      "quote_verified": true
    },
    {
      "kind": "chewy_protection",
