      "section": "Section 1.01 (definition of Excluded Subsidiary)",
      "quote": "Notwithstanding the foregoing, no Domestic Subsidiary that becomes an Excluded Subsidiary pursuant to clause (b) of this definition shall be deemed to be an Excluded Subsidiary except as a result of a transaction permitted under this Agreement resulting in some of the Equity Interests of such Domestic Subsidiary becoming owned by an unaffiliated third party that is for a bona fide business purpose and not primarily for the purpose of releasing Collateral.",
      "summary": "A domestic guarantor that stops being wholly owned becomes an Excluded Subsidiary, and is released, only if the equity went to an unaffiliated third party for a bona fide business purpose and not primarily to release collateral.",
